@@ -1,18 +1,3 @@
-From e0d482fdcfe92046f9d32e00624014c31576be6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
-From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
-Date: Sun, 5 Feb 2017 17:55:53 +0100
-Subject: [PATCH] rt2x00: mt7620: differentiate based on SoC CHIP_VER
-
-The vendor driver does things differently based on what it finds in the
-SoC's CHIP_VER register, which tells whether this is MT7620N or MT7620A
-(PKG) and most likely also the revision (VER) and something about the
-silicon implementer (ECO). Introduce codepaths just like the ones in
-the vendor driver to handle the different chips properly. Some of those
-paths are most likely dead code left over from FPGA versions or early
-prototypes of the chip.
-
-Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
